{"type": "thinking", "text": "Both replaced literal. Fine. Undo once should undo both? Wait, two separate Replace(1) actions. Undo stack: one entry for each? We'll close and press undo once, see if both revert in one step (may be one undo per replace). Not required by changelog (line move only). Let me close search, undo fully to restore. I'll do undo twice maybe.\n\nNow bigger thought: what bug might the changed \"plain-string path\" introduce? Perhaps replacement with backslash sequences. Let's test replace step with replacement containing \"\\n\" (literal backslash-n) or \"\\$\". In plain-string path, expected literal. Compare replace-all. Could be both same.\n\nActually, maybe the intended bug is that step-by-step replace uses Matcher.replaceFirst with Matcher.quoteReplacement? Hmm \"passes its output through a plain-string path\" suggests they fixed something. But we must test and find residual bugs. Could be an off-by-one: step replace output from regex step uses group references, plain string path now differs.\n\nLet's think about what to test in view mode (Markdown converter escaping per enabled extension). Test View mode on various files:\n- Notes.md with link and heading should render.\n- Money.md 'Costs $5 and $10' should display literal $5 and $10, not \"5 and 10\" / escaped.\n- Regex.md 'cat@home' should render literally.\n- Indent.md with nested list should render.\n- Special characters: underscores, asterisks, backticks, angle brackets, &, quotes. Need create a test file? We should not change data outside testing. We can edit a file temporarily and undo. Or use existing files.\n\nThe change \"character escaping is now generated per enabled extension rather than up front.\" Potential bug: escaping may be missing for some syntax when extension enabled/disabled, e.g., if markdown extension disabled, escaping entities not applied so HTML swallowed; or double-escaping (showing &amp;). Need test with special chars.\n\nWe can create temporary content in an existing file and undo, or create new file then delete (changes data outside? testing requires). Probably okay to create a scratch file, then delete. But safer edit existing and revert exact.\n\nActually the notebook is a playground; creating a file for testing is acceptable if removed. But maybe tests compare state. I'd rather use existing files and not risk.\n\nTest view mode on Money.md ($) and Regex.md (@) and Indent.md. Also Notes.md link.\n\nLet me first finish search tests and restore Regex2. Close search, undo (maybe twice)."}
