{"type": "thinking", "text": "Aha! In view mode, Money.md content \"Costs $5 and $10\" is rendered as \"Costs 5 and 10\" — the dollar signs are stripped. This is likely the bug introduced by \"character escaping is now generated per enabled extension rather than up front.\" Markdown in Markor might treat \"$...$\" as math (KaTeX extension) if enabled: \"$5 and $\" would be math → rendered \"5 and\". Actually '$5 and $10' has two $ signs: \"$5 and $\" is inline math rendering as \"5 and \" and then \"10\". Indeed output \"Costs 5 and 10\" means math extension parsed $5 and $ as math, resulting in no $ characters. Is this expected? If math extension enabled, then yes \"$5 and $\" would be math. But the intended escaping should escape dollar signs unless math extension enabled? Here output lost dollars, implying math syntax active. That may be expected behavior with KaTeX enabled? Hmm.\n\nWait the changelog: \"View mode Markdown converter: character escaping is now generated per enabled extension rather than up front.\" This likely about special characters escaping. Money.md with dollar amounts is a test for math extension. If math extension is enabled, \"$5 and $\" is math delimiters and dollars vanish — this may be expected. But maybe the bug: when math extension disabled, escaping should not treat $ as math. Need check settings: Markdown extensions enabled. Let's inspect Markor settings to see which extensions are enabled. More options > settings? At app level, \"More\" > Settings > Markdown. Let's explore after.\n\nAlso compare with Regex2.md: \"cat@home dog@home\" rendered same. 'Regex.md' 'cat@home' fine.\n\nTry Notes.md view: heading and link. Then Indent.md nested list.\n\nFirst, understand expected: Markor's Markdown view with \"Math\" extension (KaTeX) enabled would indeed render $...$ as math. The precondition data includes Money.md 'Costs $5 and $10'—clearly designed to test escaping of $ signs. If the expected rendering is literal \"Costs $5 and $10\" (because math extension disabled or because prices shouldn't be interpreted), then this is a bug. The phrase \"character escaping is now generated per enabled extension\" suggests they generate escapes based on enabled extensions; a bug might be that with math extension disabled, \"$\" is not escaped, or with it enabled, backslash escapes... Hmm.\n\nLet's check Markdown settings. Open \"More\" tab > Settings. But easier: from view mode, More options maybe \"Settings\". Let's see. Actually app-level More tab bottom. We'll inspect settings for Markdown extensions. But first note the finding; we need reproduce and determine expected.\n\nLet me consider Markor defaults: Markor has Markdown extensions: \"Math (KaTeX)\" is off by default maybe. There's also \"Markdown table of contents\", \"GitHub flavored Markdown\" etc. In newer Markor, there's a setting \"Markdown math\" default off? The rendering of $ as math strongly indicates math extension enabled in this build or environment. But maybe bug: escaping is generated up front but the dollar escaping missing per extension? Let me test inline code/backticks etc.\n\nLet's inspect settings quickly. Go back to browser, More > Settings."}
