{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed: with no checkbox = OFF; tapping row = ON. So math was OFF when QAtmp rendered \"A x^2 B and Costs 5 and 10 C\"! Wait, we need to recheck timeline carefully:\n\nTimeline:\n- First settings visit (before any toggle): no checkbox → math OFF.\n- Tapped row → checkbox checked → math ON.\n- Tapped checkbox → disappeared → math OFF.\n- Viewed Money → \"Costs 5 and 10\" while math OFF. Hmm that's the bug then.\n- Later checked settings again: no checkbox (OFF) confirmed.\n- Viewed Notes (no $) fine.\n- Created QAtmp and viewed while OFF → dollars stripped.\n\nWait but maybe the initial state after app launch was math ON?? The observe before first tap had no CheckBox, and we've now established that checkbox present = ON. Thus initial OFF. Then tapping turned ON, then off. So Money viewed with OFF and stripped. So there is a bug: dollar signs are being treated as math even when Math extension is disabled. But hold on—for QAtmp, did we view before or after this last toggle ON? Timeline: QAtmp view happened before this latest settings visit. At that time, after the second toggle off, math was OFF. So yes, OFF and stripped.\n\nHmm, but could the settings reader cache at process level such that turning ON then OFF...? When we viewed Money after toggling off, math was off. When app restarted? We didn't kill. But the activity recreated. Preferences maybe cached in static field `AppSettings` loaded on process start; toggles might update it. Hmm.\n\nBut now math is ON. Let's view QAtmp now to see the difference. If ON yields same \"A x^2 B and Costs 5 and 10 C\" then the toggle has no effect at all (possible bug), confirming math handling always on. If ON yields e.g. rendered math with spacing (no x^2?), maybe different.\n\nLet's navigate to QAtmp and view."}
