{"type": "thinking", "text": "With math ON, QAtmp view shows \"A \" then math views (x^2) then \" B and Costs \" then math 5 ... then \"10 C\". So the dollar-delimited math is rendered as generated math. So with math ON, dollars become math. Fine.\n\nEarlier with OFF it showed a single TextView \"A x^2 B and Costs 5 and 10 C\", also dollars stripped. So math OFF still strips dollars?! Hmm wait—no. When math off, the display \"A x^2 B and Costs 5 and 10 C\" still had no dollars. That seems wrong. Unless... when we viewed it with OFF, perhaps the math setting was actually ON because our second toggle turned it on? Let's re-derive from the checkbox observations:\n\n- At first Markdown settings (before toggling): no checkbox → is that OFF or hidden?\n- Tapped row → checkbox [checked].\n- Tapped checkbox → no checkbox.\n- Later, no checkbox. Tapped row → checkbox [checked].\n- Now ON.\n\nIf no checkbox means OFF, then check states sequence: OFF → ON → OFF → OFF → ON. So QAtmp first view was OFF, and dollars stripped. That would be contradictory to math ON test where it showed math nodes. Actually wait, maybe when OFF, the converter still treats `$...$` as math? That's precisely the bug. But then with ON, it renders as math *views* (different HTML). Both remove dollars; difference is only in KaTeX rendering. Hmm, if math is OFF, why would there be math conversion at all? But the output \"A x^2 B and Costs 5 and 10 C\" is plain text with dollars removed. If math OFF, the escaping logic might still *escape* the `$` characters (to avoid math) by removing them? Escaping in HTML should be `\\$`? No.\n\nWait, maybe with math OFF, `$` is treated as Markdown \"math\" still? No.\n\nAlternatively, the OFF rendering might have been a cached previous view? No, separate.\n\nLet me now toggle OFF again and view QAtmp, carefully verifying state, to confirm. Current math ON. Go settings, tap checkbox to OFF, then view QAtmp. Then compare. Do it methodically."}
