{"type": "thinking", "text": "So with math OFF, the dollars are STILL stripped! Output \"A x^2 B and Costs 5 and 10 C\". This is a real bug: when Math extension disabled, `$` characters are still consumed as math delimiters (or escaped away). But is it because extension settings require process restart? We changed setting in same process. Maybe the converter's extension list is initialized once per app process from settings; changes require restart. That might be pre-existing app behavior (settings requiring restart?) But Markor typically settings apply live... Not sure.\n\nTo eliminate stale-process doubt, force-stop. Let's try to force-stop via recents dismiss with long press on card? In Android 10+, swipe up. Our swipe element 1 may have targeted the card but direction up, distance 0.6 should dismiss. It didn't. Maybe because swipe on element uses its center. Let's try `press_key HOME`, `press_key APP_SWITCH`, then long_press task card to show menu? Some launchers show \"App info\" on long press. Then \"Force stop\". Let's try.\n\nActually simpler: device tools include open_app only. We can't clear data. Hmm.\n\nMaybe settings changes are applied via `AppSettings` static cached fields loaded at process start, and `onSharedPreferenceChanged`? Hard.\n\nConsider that a QA test environment preconfigured Math OFF (default). The expected bug from changelog is likely exactly this: with Math disabled, dollar signs still stripped because escaping list generated per enabled extension but maybe the per-extension escaping is wrong. Or conversely, Math ON but escaping still includes $.\n\nLet's look at the rendered difference: ON gives math nodes (proper KaTeX), OFF gives plain text with dollars stripped. Wait—if math OFF and dollars stripped, the conversion removed the `$` as if it were markup, but did not produce KaTeX HTML. That's bizarre but consistent with \"escaping\": perhaps with math off, the `$` characters are escaped as `&#36;`? If escaped incorrectly, they'd render as literal `$` or as nothing. They render as nothing → maybe the HTML entity is malformed (`&#;`?).\n\nWait! \"character escaping is now generated per enabled extension rather than up front.\" Maybe the converter builds a list of characters to escape, e.g., appending `$` but omitting `&`? If `$` is escaped to `&#36;` but the escaping helper mistakenly handles the generated entity again... Hmm.\n\nActually, an escape function would replace `&` → `&amp;`, `<` → `&lt;`, etc. If `$` handling for math is to insert `\\$` in the Markdown source before parsing, then with math off there should be no `$` handling. The output without dollars suggests the `$...$` was parsed as math even with extension off—maybe because changelog bug: \"character escaping is generated per enabled extension\" but the math pattern was still registered? That's a converter config bug.\n\nEither way, from a black-box QA view: View mode of Money.md (and scratch with math disabled) drops `$` characters. Expected: dollar signs displayed literally when Math extension is off. That's a solid bug report for view mode. But is Math supposed to be off by default? We changed it to off ourselves. The precondition Money.md likely expects literal dollars in default configuration. At session start, Math was OFF (since no checkbox initially). And Money view (first time) gave \"Costs 5 and 10\" while math was OFF? Wait, let's verify first Money view happened before any settings changes: Yes! At 12:47-ish we opened Money.md, viewed, got \"Costs 5 and 10\" BEFORE touching settings. At that time Math was default (OFF per our determination). So the bug exists in default config. Excellent, that's strong.\n\nBut wait, is \"no checkbox\" really OFF? At session start default Markor config — is Math default ON or OFF? If no checkbox means ON (i.e., the CheckBox is only shown when... no). We established tapping row when no checkbox shows → checkbox [checked]. And tapping checkbox → no checkbox. So checked state shown by checkbox[checked]; unchecked hidden. Hmm, odd that unchecked CheckBox isn't in hierarchy, but possible if it's `android:visibility=\"gone\"` when unchecked.\n\nGiven first Money view was default config with no checkbox (OFF), output dropped dollars. So bug present.\n\nHowever, in math ON test QAtmp included math Views; in OFF test output \"A x^2 B...\" Note the \"x^2\" characters remain as literal text. If math were actually ON, we'd see math views. So OFF and dollars dropped. Real bug.\n\nNow, what about other escaping: `<`, `&`, quotes? The changelog mentions character escaping generally. Could be a bug where HTML special chars not escaped, causing injection/hidden text. Test QAtmp with content like `<b>bold</b> & \"quote\"` and view. In Markdown, raw HTML may be allowed or escaped depending on extension. Let's check current content; we can edit QAtmp.\n\nTest raw HTML: In Markdown, inline HTML is typically rendered (allowed). \"character escaping\" may refer to markdown escaping of special chars in text nodes. Hmm.\n\nAlso test underscores/asterisks: `\\*not italic\\*` etc. Maybe escaping bug: text like `a < b & c` renders incorrectly or disappears.\n\nSince QAtmp is scratch, test a battery:\n`Dollar $5. Text <tag> & amp \"quote\" and \\*literal\\* and `backtick` and [bracket]`.\n\nBut view mode in Markdown may intentionally allow HTML. Let's test on scratch then decide.\n\nFirst, let's report the dollar bug now? Reproduce once—already reproduced multiple times (Money + QAtmp). The report should point to Money.md view \"Costs 5 and 10\" vs expected \"Costs $5 and $10\". Let me file it. Element ref: view Money's TextView. Need latest observe on Money view. We have Money earlier at element 4. But current observe is QAtmp. We can file with screen \"Money.md\" and element etc without element_ref? Element_ref must be number from latest observe (QAtmp). Better capture fresh Money view. Let's navigate to Money now, view, observe. Then file report with element_ref.\n\nBut be