{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now Money view shows \"Costs 5 and 10\" while Math is OFF (we just turned it off and confirmed). Also at session start it showed the same. This is clearly a real escaping bug: dollar signs removed even with math disabled. But wait—could it be that the setting is OFF but the app's converter extension list loaded at startup retains Math ON because default config? At startup, was math on? We observed no checkbox initially, which we interpret as OFF. Hmm, but perhaps at startup math was ON, but the checkbox was hidden because the row's checkbox is only shown when the row is \"activated\"/focused? No—tapping row made it checked, so tapping toggled ON.\n\nWait, maybe tapping the row toggles and the checkbox only appears when checked (checked state = visible check mark in a widget that only draws when checked). Yes, that's what a checkbox does; the view exists always but semantics only expose it when checked. So initial = unchecked = OFF. So at session start Math OFF, and Money dropped $. Bug.\n\nBut hmm, there's still a possibility the initial Money view was before app-config load? No.\n\nLet's test with Math ON again Money should show math nodes (dollars still gone). Current is OFF. Good.\n\nNow, is the expected behavior for Money with Math OFF definitely \"$5 and $10\"? Yes, if math extension disabled, dollar signs should be literal. The dollar signs disappearing is data loss in display. This is strong. Let's file.\n\nReport:\nscreen \"Money.md (View Mode)\"\nelement \"Document preview text\"\nfield \"document content\"\nsymptom_type \"wrong_value\"\nexpected \"The preview shows 'Costs $5 and $10' preserving the dollar signs, because the Markdown Math extension is disabled.\"\nobserved \"The preview displays 'Costs 5 and 10' — both '$' characters are dropped.\"\nsteps: open Files > Money.md, ensure Settings > Markdown > Math is off, tap View Mode.\nelement_ref 4, observed_quote \"Costs 5 and 10\".\n\nLet me file."}
