{"type": "thinking", "text": "Escaped backslashes work perfectly, including single \\$5 preserved. Interesting! So single $5 appears literally when escaped. The Money issue might be that an even number of $ is interpreted as math regardless of extension setting. With math off, `\\$5` preserved as $5. Hmm, escaping did work.\n\nWait, this shows `$5` (escaped) preserved. In earlier QAtmp with math OFF, unescaped `$x^2$` and `$5 ... $10` lost dollars. So paired dollars trigger math conversion even with Math OFF. If Math OFF but KaTeX conversion still occurs... Hmm. But maybe math extension on/off only affects whether KaTeX renders, but the markdown parser always treats `$...$` as math? That's not expected.\n\nHold on: did we verify math is currently off? We turned it off before viewing QAtmp. Since then we changed nothing. Current view math off. The escaped test shows $5 preserved because escaped. The unescaped paired $ gets consumed. So math delimiters processed even when setting off. Likely bug.\n\nCould the previous QAtmp unescaped view with \"math ON\" showing math Views vs OFF showing plain text with dollars gone be due to stale doc? Wait with ON it produced View nodes (KaTeX); with OFF plain TextView. Both dollars gone. So when OFF, the `$...$` was still parsed as math but rendered as plain text? That seems weird but possible if the Markdown parser always produces math nodes and the math extension setting only controls KaTeX rendering (rendering as plain text fallback). That would be a real design/config bug: disabling math should treat $ as literal.\n\nEither way, Money.md expected literal dollars. Our report stands confirmed by developer. Good.\n\nNow cleanup QAtmp: delete via file browser long press. Let's do that before continuing, to restore data. Back to browser, long press QAtmp."}
