{"type": "thinking", "text": "QAtmp deleted. Good.\n\nNow other tests:\n\n1. File browser sort with Folder first toggled and reverse. Check \"reverse kept alongside chosen key\" maybe also when choosing \"Folder local\" (the first option, maybe a different sort grouping). Could test \"Folder local\" + reverse. But main issue done. Check cancel behaves: change sort then CANCEL → order unchanged and previous settings preserved. We tested cancel leaves prior state. Maybe verify: after setting Name+reverse, cancel while selecting Size left Name reverse. Reopen showed Name+reverse? We didn't verify after cancel, but likely.\n\n2. State persistence after app kill: sort remains. Could test by leaving app and coming back; we did navigate but not kill. Maybe enough.\n\n3. Editing actions: line move up/down undo one step done. Also duplicate line action maybe. Test duplicate works and undo. Not changed but editing actions area. Could check.\n\n4. Search/replace: step replace path bug found. Other search features: match case, whole word, regex, find in selection, line-based search. We might test \"Match Case\" toggle state and behavior. But scope is search/replace dialog.\n\nPotential bug: result count \"No results\" stale. We noticed this twice: after typing a search term with matches, the label still says \"No results\" until Next/Previous pressed. Is that a real user-visible bug? On first search opening, after typing \"guide\", label \"No results\"; pressing Next shows 1/2. If the count doesn't auto-update until navigation, it's a minor bug. In many editors the result count updates as you type. This could be pre-existing and not related to changelog, but QA sweep should catch. Is it worth reporting? Possibly. But precision matters: developer may reject as \"expected until navigation\". Hmm.\n\nLet me examine more carefully: after typing \"home\" the result remains \"1/1\" from previous search — stale, definitely misleading. That's a bug: result indicator doesn't refresh on text change. But maybe typing via automation doesn't trigger the TextWatcher that updates? It should. The label updates when regex toggle clicked. Hmm. Could be a real bug.\n\nHowever, the changelog doesn't mention search count; focus changed area \"search and replace dialog: step-by-step replace plain-string path\". Reporting unrelated pre-existing minor UI issue might be okay but may be considered noise. The instruction: \"sweep these areas before release\" and \"signing off while bugs remain is worst\". The result indicator is part of search/replace area. I'd report if reproducible robustly and clearly wrong. Let me test again cleanly with a fresh search: open Notes search, type \"e\", observe count. Maybe the first type char updates? Let's test later. Could be related to automation: type_text might set text without triggering afterTextChanged? But UI updates selection highlight? Let's check visual highlight in screenshot maybe. Observe after typing \"guide\" showed \"No results\". If highlight existed maybe count stale.\n\nLet's test using individual key typing? too tedious. type_text likely sends text input events, triggering TextWatcher. Hmm.\n\nLet's reproduce cleanly on Money or Notes: open search (fresh), type \"e\", observe result. If \"No results\" while many matches → bug. But when the search field is empty, \"No results\" maybe expected; after typing should update. It didn't for cat/home. This is reproducible.\n\nYet, maybe Markor intentionally only computes on Next/Prev for performance. But then \"No results\" is misleading. The developer may or may not confirm. I'd lean to report as minor bug since it's user-visible and in area.\n\nBut first let's test other things: rotate device. Rotate on file browser and editor; check content preserved.\n\nTest rotate in editor with unsaved changes? We can type something, rotate, verify text remains, undo. Let's do in Notes.md or Regex2.\n\nAlso check \"view mode\" device rotation: rotate while viewing Notes, check render.\n\nAlso test search/replace cancel: cancel closes dialog and doesn't modify. Fine.\n\nAlso editing line actions with indentation: Indent.md move lines? The change is undo one step; we verified with Notes. Maybe test Indent2 where lines have indentation, move up/down preserves text.\n\nAlso \"Duplicate (Ctrl+D)\" could be part of editing actions. Test quickly.\n\nLet's prioritize:\nA. File browser sort: done mostly. Maybe test \"Folder first\" unchecked with reverse + name; and sort persistence across app restart. We'll do a couple.\nB. Editor line actions undo (done up/down). Maybe test repeated move (move down twice then single undo?). Let's test \"move down twice, undo once\" should revert only last move? Each action one undo step. That's fine. Not necessary.\nC. Search/replace: step replace bug reported; test cancel/no-op; result count maybe.\nD. View mode: dollar bug reported; test rotation, extension toggling, maybe TOC? Not necessary.\n\nLet's test rotation in editor and view quickly.\n\nOpen Notes.md, type \"X\" maybe, rotate landscape, check text, undo. Actually we don't want to leave changes; undo. Alternatively rotation alone with no changes. Let's test rotation with view mode first: open Notes view, rotate landscape, verify content still renders.\n\nFrom browser, open Notes, it opens in view mode (last mode for Notes? earlier we used view). Let's tap Notes."}
