{"type": "thinking", "text": "Whoa! Move line up on \"- a\\n  - deep\\n\" produced \"- a\\n\\n  - deep\" — it inserted a blank line and removed the trailing newline, instead of swapping lines to \"  - deep\\n- a\\n\". This is a significant bug! Wait, maybe the cursor wasn't on second line but at end of second line? The move line up should swap line 2 with line 1. Result \"- a\\n\\n  - deep\" is wrong: it seems \"deep\" line moved up? Let's think:\n\nOriginal: line1 \"- a\", line2 \"  - deep\", line3 \"\" (trailing).\nIf cursor on line2, move up → line1 \"  - deep\", line2 \"- a\", line3 \"\". Expected in text: \"  - deep\\n- a\\n\". Got \"- a\\n\\n  - deep\". That looks like line2 content was cleared and reinserted at end? Actually \"- a\\n\\n  - deep\" = line1 \"- a\", line2 empty, line3 \"  - deep\". So the second line moved down to line3, not up! That's the opposite direction? Hmm.\n\nWait maybe the tap at (300,360) placed cursor on line 3 (empty trailing line), so move line up would swap line3 with line2 → \"- a\\n\\n  - deep\" (empty line moves above deep). Yes! That's exactly correct for moving line3 up. Because the editor's line 3 is empty (trailing newline). So the cursor was on line 3 empty, move up swapped it with line2. So result is coherent.\n\nHmm. Hard to place cursor on second line. Text lines likely at y≈299 and 346? EditText center 346? Let's screenshot after? Not worth. The undo works one step; tap undo."}
