{"type": "thinking", "text": "After wait, it updated to \"2/2\". So it's a debounce; not a bug. Good not report.\n\nNow close search. The search counted 2/2 which is correct.\n\nNext: consider \"Search and replace\" specifics: empty search, replace all with empty fields? Boundary: Pressing Replace with empty search does nothing. Fine.\n\nTest \"Match Case\" behavior maybe. Not necessary.\n\nTest file browser sort \"reverse kept alongside sort key\" more: We already saw Date+reverse then Name+reverse, and reverse persisted. But what about the reverse toggle when choosing \"Name\" from menu while reverse checked—stayed checked. Confirmed.\n\nBut perhaps bug: after choosing a sort key, reverse gets cleared when reopening if selection made via tapping? We tested: selected Date then Reverse, OK; reopen showed Date+Reverse. Then selected Name, OK; reopen showed Name+Reverse. Good.\n\nTest \"Folder first\" + reverse interactions maybe: With reverse on, folder first still showed Zeta at top. Is that expected? \"Folder first\" should keep folder before files regardless of reverse, probably yes. In reverse name order we got Zeta, todo, Single... folder first. Good.\n\nTest \"Folder local\" option? Might be \"sort by folder local\"? Not needed.\n\nNow view mode more: test Math on (which is current? we left math OFF after last toggle; during the QAtmp escaped test math OFF). We need restore default? Default was OFF (initial). Fine, leave OFF.\n\nTest TOC with headings? Notes has one heading. Not necessary.\n\nTest front matter? Not data.\n\nTest View mode on todo.txt? Not markdown.\n\nTest escaping of `&` etc already good.\n\nPotential other view bug: Markdown converter with enabled extension when \"Math\" ON and `$` pairs; expected math. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: Table of contents or \"*\" lists? Indent works.\n\nTest \"view mode rotation\" done.\n\nNow editing actions: test line movement undo as one step again with non-empty lines and check just one undo restores (done twice). Good.\n\nTest undo after line move + check redo restores moved state. Could be worthwhile: move down, undo, redo. Let's test on Notes quickly maybe. But Notes content restored and undo history? We left Notes with an undo step (from typing/deleting) maybe history persisted. Could complicate. Use Indent2: move line down then undo/redo.\n\nCurrently search open in Indent2. Close, move line. Let's do: close search, tap first line, Special Key Move down; observe, undo; then redo. This tests reversal doubly. But we've already verified undo; redo isn't required by changelog. Maybe skip.\n\nMore important: editing actions menu itself includes \"Duplicate (Ctrl + D)\" and moving line up/down; test duplicate on Indent2? Not changed. Scope \"editing actions and search/replace\" might include toolbar actions (bold, lists, indent). But the changed line is the undo-step behavior. We did enough.\n\nHowever, there's a potential bug: after moving a line, the undo entry count. We verified one undo restores both directions. Good.\n\nNow file browser: search icon in file browser maybe global search across files. Area \"file browser and its sort options\" maybe includes file search? Not necessarily. Could test \"Go to\" and breadcrumb. We navigated folder Zeta and back. Good.\n\nCould test rename/delete? Not sort. Avoid data change.\n\nNow think about \"reverse option kept alongside chosen sort key\" - maybe bug when toggling reverse alone and then selecting same key: after setting Name+reverse, selecting Name again should it keep reverse? We saw selecting different key keeps reverse. Fine.\n\nWhat about Cancel: If user changes Folder first or reverse then Cancel, state should remain previous. We tested Cancel after selecting Size (before OK), then screen stayed Name reverse; but did we verify reopen after cancel? Not exactly. Let's verify now: open sort menu (currently Name+reverse), toggle Reverse off, tap CANCEL, reopen and confirm Reverse still checked. This tests cancel semantics. Let's do.\n\nCurrently in Indent2 search. Close search, back to browser. Actually sort menu available in browser. Let's go back. Close search first (tap element 5)."}
