{"type": "thinking", "text": "Ascending restored. Note Notes.md modified time 12:56 (from our editing); unavoidable because we changed and restored content but mtime changed. That's testing side effect; acceptable.\n\nNow file browser with sort tested thoroughly.\n\nRemaining: maybe test file browser search? \"the file browser and its sort options\" — I'd interpret sort options only. We did.\n\nPotential sort bug: The reverse option kept alongside chosen key works, but what if you choose a sort key while Reverse is on, does the list actually apply reverse *for the new key*? We tested Name and got reverse. Date reverse with identical dates inconclusive. Size? All files may have different sizes; could test Size+reverse; but not needed.\n\nNow view mode: maybe test TOC extension? Not in data.\n\nLet's revisit the Money bug to ensure it's not impacted by a stale Math setting in converter. The developer confirmed it, so fine.\n\nCould there be another view mode bug relating to \"per enabled extension\" like escaping of `\\` when Math on? We tested \\$5 with math off shows $5; with math off unescaped pair gets eaten. That's the reported bug.\n\nMaybe test with Math ON a single escaped \\$5 — should show $5 not math; fine.\n\nWhat about Markdown line with `cat@home dog@home` view — shows fine. Notes link fine.\n\nMaybe view mode should render GFM \"strikethrough\" etc not relevant.\n\nNow editing search/replace: maybe test \"replace all\" with `$1` regex off—literal. We tested step off literal; all off not tested but probably literal. The step-vs-all discrepancy with regex on is reported.\n\nCould there be a bug where step replace doesn't update match count/selection? We saw it updates count to 1/1 after first replace. Fine.\n\nCould there be a bug where Replace (1) on same match repeated? No.\n\nPotential bug with \"Replace (1)\" when regex enabled and replacement contains backslash? The confirmed report covers.\n\nLet's test \"Match Case\" + \"Whole Word\" behavior? Maybe not required. But \"Search and replace dialog\" area—could be extensive. The changed part is step-by-step replace plain-string. We covered.\n\nNow maybe test editing actions: undo/redo of line moving with Redo. We confirmed undo; redo enabled after undo? In Notes earlier redo enabled. Could test redo once returns moved state. Let's verify quickly in Indent2? We restored. Might not be needed but reversal criterion says check redo returns right state. Let's test with a simple move on Indent2: place line1, move down, undo, redo, observe. Then undo again.\n\nWe already have tool routines. But it costs steps. We have plenty. Let's do to be thorough.\n\nCurrently browser. Open Indent2."}
