{"type": "thinking", "text": "Place cursor line1, move down, undo, redo. That's several calls; maybe skip since redo is not changed. We've verified enough.\n\nActually, the task emphasizes \"Reversal: undo, cancel or reverse a change, and check the app returns to the right state.\" We tested undo both directions and cancel. Good.\n\nNow consider the \"file browser sort menu reverse kept alongside chosen sort key\" could have a subtle bug: when you reopen the sort menu after choosing a *different* key with reverse on, reverse shows checked. Verified. What about after rotating? Not relevant.\n\nLet's test navigation by more than one route: open file from file browser vs from To-Do? To-Do only todo.txt. View mode from file browser is the route. Search results? Eh.\n\nPotential bug in editor: Save button state after edits. Earlier, typing changed content but Save remained disabled; is that a bug? Wait observe after typing \"TEST\" showed Save disabled and Undo disabled until we pressed DEL, then both enabled. This might be an artifact of `type_text` injecting text without triggering TextWatcher immediately? But the text clearly changed. If Save is disabled, are changes persisted? In Markor, auto-save is always on, so Save button may be disabled intentionally? Actually Save button desc \"Save\" enabled/disabled indicates dirty state. If text changes but Save remains disabled, maybe it auto-saves instantly, so nothing to save. Undo enabled eventually. Hmm.\n\nDoes Markor auto-save? I think Markor saves automatically on pause and has a Save button that is always enabled? In our initial editor, Save disabled. After line move, Save disabled too (auto-save?). So Save seems rarely enabled. Not a good bug.\n\nData consistency: after editing and restoring, file browser timestamps updated for Notes. Fine.\n\nNow, perhaps check file content persistence: open Notes again verify original (it showed original in edit). Yes.\n\nOne more important test: line move undo step when moving up at top boundary (no previous line) should do nothing / no undo entry. If it creates an empty undo step or corrupts, that's a bug. Test on Notes: cursor on line1, Move up → should no-op; then Undo should be disabled (or undo previous unrelated? undo history empty). Let's test on Indent2 line1: Move up at top; expect content unchanged and undo disabled. Do it. Currently Indent2 editor, tap line1, Move up."}
