llar signs, but that's how Math syntax works. The precondition Money.md likely tests literal display regardless of math setting? Hmm, maybe with Math ON `$5 and $10` should also show literal dollars because the dollar pair is not valid math? KaTeX would still render it. Not our concern; we filed the Math off case.\n\nWait, maybe initial default Math was ON, not OFF, because the initial Money view at session start dropped dollars. Then we toggled to... Let's re-derive once more, because if initial state was ON and we left it OFF, we'd be leaving a changed setting! That's important for data restoration. Let's verify checkbox semantics explicitly:\n\nObservation A (first Markdown settings, before any tap): elements list did NOT include CheckBox.\nObservation B (after tapping row): CheckBox id=checkbox [checked] appeared.\nObservation C (after tapping checkbox): CheckBox gone.\n\nDoes absence mean unchecked or \"not rendered\"? In Android, CheckBox widget in a preference row is always present; the accessibility tree usually includes it even when unchecked. But this harness lists only meaningful elements; an unchecked CheckBox might still be listed as \"CheckBox id=checkbox\". Why would it vanish? Possibly because the checkbox is `android:visibility=\"gone\"` when unchecked, and `visible` when checked. That is plausible: the row shows a checkmark icon only if checked.\n\nThus A = unchecked, B = checked, C = unchecked. So initial = OFF. And we left OFF. Good.\n\nBut wait, in observation A the list had 11 elements and no checkbox; maybe if unchecked the CheckBox is still present but *not clickable* and not exposed? The harness lists TextView labels etc. Unlikely to omit. Another way to confirm: current state after our last visit is OFF, and we observed no checkbox. If we now check the setting and tap the row, checkbox appears. We did that. So no-checkbox = unchecked. Initial no-checkbox = unchecked = OFF. Good. Left OFF.\n\nAnd the Money bug appears with Math OFF at both session start and later. Solid.\n\nNow perhaps run one final verification of the two bugs before sign-off? Already confirmed by developer. No need.\n\nBut wait, there's a potential third bug I noticed: When the Math extension is OFF, the view mode presumably uses escaping, but the *dollar* issue. That's one. Could the intended \"character escaping generated per enabled extension\" also affect escaping of `<`/`&` when \"Math\" enabled? E.g., with Math ON, HTML tags maybe not escaped? We tested HTML with Math OFF (raw tags rendered bold because Markdown allows inline HTML). With Math ON maybe escaping changes? The escaping is probably about `&` etc. But raw HTML is expected to render in Markdown. Hmm.\n\nLet's test view mode with Math ON and QAtmp-style content? QAtmp deleted. Could use Notes? Not necessary.\n\nGiven the developer confirmed both, and we have tested all specified areas reasonably, proceed to sign off. But before sign-off, check all data states:\n- Notes content original (confirmed).\n- Regex2 original (confirmed after undo; but then we made no further edits? We later opened Regex2 and did empty replace then undo. Yes restored).\n- Indent2 original after messy restoration. We should verify once more maybe by viewing tree: we left Indent2 at \"- a\\n  - deep\\n\" and backed out. Then opened Notes. Let's reopen Indent2 quickly to confirm (it's at top). Actually last content observed in browser mtime 1:00 and we saw \"- a\\n  - deep\\n\" in the final editor before backing out. It auto-saved. Good.\n- Money untouched.\n- Single, Regex, etc untouched.\n- QAtmp deleted.\n- Math OFF initial.\n- Sort Name/Folder first/no reverse initial.\n\nOne thing: In the file browser, the sort dialog \"Folder local\" was toggled then Cancel — cancel discards; fine.\n\nI should maybe verify that no QAtmp remains: current browser lists Indent2, Indent, Money, Notes, Regex2, Regex, Shopping, Single, todo + Zeta. No QAtmp. Good.\n\nLet me open Indent2 one more time to verify content exact, then back. Actually current state at Notes editor; back to browser; tap Indent2. Quick."}
