{"type": "thinking", "text": "Restored Name ascending. Good.\n\nNow, one more thought: The \"Folder local\" option is weird but not our focus. Could there be a bug: selecting \"Folder local\" along with Name shows both checked, which might be intended as separate setting (\"Folder local\" maybe a filter?). Not reporting.\n\nWe've done many tests. Let's consider view mode default extension: the Math setting OFF is initial. Did our test of switching Math ON/OFF and back to OFF leave any other View Mode setting changed? We only toggled Math. Fine.\n\nCould our toggling \"Folder local\" and cancel have altered something? Cancel no.\n\nCould our sort default originally have \"Folder local\" checked? At session start sort dialog: Folder local not checked. Now same (cancel). Good.\n\nNow maybe run a final verification of the two bugs after all this? The developer already confirmed; no need.\n\nSign off? Before that, reflect if there's a third bug in changed areas I might be missing. Let's scrutinize the changelog items:\n\n1. Editor line actions menu: moving line up/down one undo step. Tested:\n   - Move down (Notes) → undo one step restored.\n   - Move up (Notes) → undo one step restored.\n   - Indent2: move down twice → undo once reverted only second. Good.\n   - Boundary move up at top no-op.\n   Looks solid.\n\n2. Search and replace dialog: step-by-step replace output plain-string path. Found bug with regex $1 vs replace all. The developer confirmed. Could there also be an issue that the *plain-string path* means replacement text containing `$` or `\\` is handled literally (intended) but also maybe the *replaced match text* gets mangled for Unicode or newline? We tested $1. Good.\n\n3. View mode Markdown converter: character escaping per enabled extension. Found $ dollar bug with math off. Could there be a second escaping bug involving backslash? Tested escaped chars display correctly. Could there be bug with `&` or `<`? Tested, displayed literally/HTML as expected. Could there be double-escaping of `&amp;`? Let's test: content `&amp;` should display `&` (Markdown HTML entity) or literal \"&amp;\"? Standard Markdown converts entity to &, so either could be correct. Not a clear bug.\n\nCould there be bug with quotes/smart quotes? Not data.\n\n4. File browser sort: reverse kept. Tested extensively. Fine.\n\nOne thing: The precondition says \"Single.md (one line, 'gamma', with no newline at the end)\". We viewed it correctly. Maybe test that editing and saving preserves missing trailing newline? Not changed area, and risky. Skip.\n\nCould view mode omit Single content in some conditions? Screenshot showed gamma, okay.\n\nPotential issue: In view mode, Math OFF and Money loses $; also QAtmp lost $ for pair. That's enough.\n\nNow, maybe we should test \"View mode\" with the Math extension ON to see if Money is expected to show math; if with ON the money line renders as math \"Costs 5 and 10\" too, but that's expected under math syntax. Not a separate bug. But it might mean the actual bug is that Math can't be disabled at all (setting toggle ineffective for the converter until restart). Did we verify Math OFF actually disables math? With Math OFF, QAtmp showed plain TextView \"A x^2 B and Costs 5 and 10 C\" — that's not KaTeX rendering, so the setting did affect rendering. But dollar delimiters still consumed. So the bug is in escaping/parsing, not the toggle. Good.\n\nLet me consider whether this is expected Markor behavior: Markor's Markdown with KaTeX plugin disabled should not parse `$` math. The output dropping `$` is clearly wrong. Confirmed by dev.\n\nThus sign off with confidence about the two confirmed areas; note the two bugs were confirmed. The sign_off notes can mention two confirmed bugs, plus tests.\n\nBefore sign-off, ensure app state/data clean:\n- Notes/Indent2/Regex2 content restored.\n- QAtmp deleted.\n- Sort Name ascending, Folder first, reverse off.\n- Math off (initial).\n- No unsaved changes? Indent2 editor has text unchanged but undo history; save disabled. Fine. The app opens Indent2? Currently browser. Fine.\n- Files list includes all 10 preconditions + Zeta. yes.\n\nLet's do a final observe maybe open app? Not necessary.\n\nOne potential issue: The file browser sorted Name ascending but the order shows Indent2 before Indent, Regex2 before Regex (natural sort semantics). At session start the same order, so fine.\n\nI'll sign off. Confidence maybe 0.85. Notes: tested sort persistence/cancel/reverse with Name and Date, editor line move undo one step both directions and boundary, search/replace step vs all, view mode rendering with Math off/on, rotation, list/link rendering. Two confirmed bugs logged."}
